## Conventions

- Define typed job data interfaces
- Use meaningful job names
- Set appropriate retry strategies
- Implement dead letter queues for permanent failures
- Log all job lifecycle events
- Monitor queue health metrics
- Use flow for job dependencies
- Implement graceful worker shutdown
- Clean up old completed/failed jobs

## Anti-Patterns

- ❌ Processing jobs synchronously in request handlers
- ❌ No retry strategy for failed jobs
- ❌ Ignoring failed jobs
- ❌ Missing job data validation
- ❌ No concurrency limits
- ❌ Storing large data in job payload (use IDs, fetch from DB)
- ❌ No monitoring of queue health
- ❌ Missing graceful shutdown

**See also:** `resilience.mdc`, `logging.mdc`, `error-handling.mdc`
